    {
      "id": "28dbf277875776010c7c396fc27bf19ed3b3d35a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2813246011,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Sort of.  The packet in the attached PCAP was generated with a hacked version of Python libdns for testing purposes.  I don't have access to any actual traffic that includes `AMTRELAY` resource records.\n\n(This all came about because I've been using Wireshark to verify that I was synthesizing various RR record types correctly while testing some DNS message parsing code, so it's all a bit circular.)\n\nLooking at the raw bytes of the `RDATA` in the PCAP, they look correct to me, assuming that I'm reading [the RFC](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8777.html#name-amtrelay-rdata-format) correctly, and the `RDATA` format isn't very complicated.\n\n[amtrelay.pcapng](/uploads/48b94b6f0fe6316892eb9ddbd8425463/amtrelay.pcapng)",
          "author": {
            "id": 24665441,
            "username": "ipilcher",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Ian Pilcher",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/24665441/avatar.png?v=1779336503",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/ipilcher"
